  "problem": "Consider the equation in the variable $u,$ given by\n\n$$\n(q-5)u+9=0\n$$\n\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q?$\n\n$q=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n\n$$\nax=b\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and $b\\ne 0.$ If $a=0,$ then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $au=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(q-5)u+9 & =0 \\\\ (q-5)u+9-9 & =0-9 \\\\ {{(q-5)}_{\u23df}}_{a}u & ={{-9}_{\u23df}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\nq-5=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this for $q,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-5 & =0 \\\\ q & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
